{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3403","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3403","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3403\",\"parent_revision\":\"ae20f1da96a92270e37c35debc75425fe0a869b07436f9be5f36c5378b5115e9\",\"root_revision\":\"ae20f1da96a92270e37c35debc75425fe0a869b07436f9be5f36c5378b5115e9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-04\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`sam_task(action='update', append_section=..., section_content=...)` (backed by `sam_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py:append_section`) is append-only: when a task is reset to `not-started` and re-run (e.g. after a fix loop resets a review task per `dh:multi-perspective-review`/`dh:complete-implementation`'s recursive follow-up handling), the second run's `append_section` write appends its new block after the first run's stale block under the same heading, rather than replacing it.\\n\\nReproduction (two independent occurrences in one session): plan P6b323f17 (a `dh:multi-perspective-review` QG run for #3182). T3 (quality review) was reset to `not-started` and re-run after a REJECT verdict was fixed; the re-run's `append_section(\\\"Review Results\\\", ...)` call concatenated its new APPROVE verdict after the stale REJECT verdict already in `context-notes`, leaving two JSON objects back-to-back under one `## Review Results` heading (unparseable as a single JSON block). The synthesizer agent hit the identical bug independently on T5 (`Punch List` section) during its own reset-and-retry.\\n\\nImpact: a section written by `append_section` cannot be safely re-written by re-running the same task \u2014 every consumer that parses that section as a single JSON block (e.g. `dh:review-synthesizer` reading `Review Results`, or anything reading `Punch List`) either fails to parse or, worse, could silently pick up stale content mixed with fresh content. In this instance, the synthesizer agent caught it correctly (by re-reading immediately after write rather than trusting `updated: true`) and worked around it via `set_fields_json` to overwrite the whole field \u2014 but that workaround requires the caller to already suspect the bug and know the exact field name backing the section.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the fix likely belongs in `append_section` itself \u2014 either add a `replace_section`-equivalent mode (mirroring `backlog_groom`'s own `replace_section` parameter, which already solves the identical problem for backlog items) or have callers whose section content is a single structured block (JSON/YAML) use `set_fields_json` directly instead of `append_section`. Exact contract is design work for grooming.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered twice during dh:multi-perspective-review QG dispatch for #3182 (plan P6b323f17, tasks T3 and T5)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-04\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ec9e12e3a017fd6e563d495ac8b889540f10f09e64abf933755aaeda2f603625\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABStov7A\"}"}